665 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1620 0 R
/E (Accurate ECG grid detection is challenging because the waveform itself overlaps and obscures the underlying grid lines. Direct grid extraction often fails in regions where the ECG trace intersects the grid, leading to inaccurate pixel-to-physical unit calibration.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
666 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1621 0 R
/E (To address this issue, the segmentation mask generated by the nnU-Net model is utilized to identify ECG signal pixels. These signal pixels are then removed through a local background reconstruction process, where each signal pixel is replaced using the intensity characteristics of neighboring non-signal pixels. This effectively restores the appearance of the original ECG paper background while preserving the grid structure.)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
667 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
